{"units": [{"id": "aute-quote14", "translation": "But he, at any rate, has strength."}, {"id": "aute-quote15", "translation": "And from it the tawny horse-cock drips."}, {"id": "auteo-orth1", "translation": "to cry aloud, to shout"}, {"id": "auteo-def1", "translation": "to cry aloud, to shout"}, {"id": "auteo-note1", "translation": "[Sept. 144 ἀϋτοῦσαι [crying aloud] for ἀπύουσαι [crying out] Seidler.]"}, {"id": "auteo-quote1", "translation": "Shouting such things."}, {"id": "auteo-quote2", "translation": "He shouts such things."}, {"id": "auteo-quote3", "translation": "And he cried out sharply."}, {"id": "auteo-quote4", "translation": "Apart from foot-scrapers and the embroidered ones, a rumor cries out."}, {"id": "auteo-quote5", "translation": "Who cries out, struck with a timely blow?"}, {"id": "auteo-quote6", "translation": "Justice, exacting what is owed, cries out loudly."}, {"id": "auteo-quote7", "translation": "I shout to the deaf."}, {"id": "auteo-word1", "translation": "crying aloud"}, {"id": "auteo-word2", "translation": "crying out"}, {"id": "autika-orth1", "translation": "immediately"}, {"id": "autika-def1", "translation": "immediately"}, {"id": "autika-quote1", "translation": "But he, taking them immediately in ignorance."}, {"id": "autika-quote2", "translation": "And one toil is immediate, the other will come."}, {"id": "autoboulos-orth1", "translation": "self-willed, acting on one's own"}, {"id": "autoboulos-def1", "translation": "self-willed, acting on one's own"}, {"id": "autoboulos-quote1", "translation": "But be self-willed; I forbid it."}, {"id": "autogenes-orth1", "translation": "born of the same race"}, {"id": "autogenes-def1", "translation": "born of the same race"}, {"id": "autogenes-quote1", "translation": "The self-born marriage of the sons of Aegyptus."}, {"id": "autodaiktoi-orth1", "translation": "slain by each other"}, {"id": "autodaiktoi-def1", "translation": "slain by each other"}, {"id": "autodaiktoi-quote1", "translation": "When they die by their own hands, slain by each other."}, {"id": "autodelos-orth1", "translation": "self-evident"}, {"id": "autodelos-def1", "translation": "self-evident"}, {"id": "autodelos-quote1", "translation": "These things are self-evident."}, {"id": "autodidaktos-orth1", "translation": "self-taught"}, {"id": "autodidaktos-def1", "translation": "self-taught"}, {"id": "autodidaktos-quote1", "translation": "The spirit within is self-taught."}, {"id": "autothen-orth1", "translation": "from there"}, {"id": "autothen-def1", "translation": "from there"}, {"id": "autothen-quote1", "translation": "Sitting (Hermann: mindful) above, somehow he brought forth his thought from there, nevertheless."}, {"id": "autothektos-orth1", "translation": "self-sharpened"}, {"id": "autothektos-def1", "translation": "self-sharpened"}, {"id": "autothektos-note1", "translation": "αὐτόθηκτον [self-sharpened] Xylander."}, {"id": "autothektos-quote1", "translation": "For taking a self-sharpened Euboean sword."}, {"id": "autothektos-word1", "translation": "self-sharpened"}, {"id": "autokletos-orth1", "translation": "self-invited, unbidden"}, {"id": "autokletos-def1", "translation": "self-invited, unbidden"}, {"id": "autokletos-quote1", "translation": "You defiled the inner chamber, self-rushing, self-invited."}, {"id": "autokranos-orth1", "translation": "self-fulfilling"}, {"id": "autokranos-def1", "translation": "bringing about its own end. Thus Aeschylus (fr. 429)."}, {"id": "autokranos-note1", "translation": "Who has mixed two words of different origin and meaning. For αὐτόκρανος [self-fulfilling] in the former sense one would rather expect αὐτόκραντος [self-fulfilling], as Aeschylus said μοιρόκραντος [fate-fulfilling] and πολεμόκραντος [war-fulfilling], not μοιρόκρανος [fate-fulfilling] and πολεμόκρανος [war-fulfilling]. What is read in Hesychius, ἐπίκρανος: ἐπιμελητής, επίχαρις [overseer, pleasing], Salmasius saw to be corrupted from ἐπιήρανος [pleasing]."}, {"id": "autokranos-quote1", "translation": "A self-fulfilling word."}, {"id": "autokranos-quote2", "translation": "Self-fulfilling: self-evident, self-accomplishing."}, {"id": "autokranos-quote3", "translation": "Self-fulfilling: self-evident, showing themselves; or a monolithic column."}, {"id": "autokranos-word1", "translation": "bringing about its own end. Thus Aeschylus"}, {"id": "autokranos-word2", "translation": "self-fulfilling"}, {"id": "autokranos-word3", "translation": "self-fulfilling"}, {"id": "autokranos-word4", "translation": "fate-fulfilling"}, {"id": "autokranos-word5", "translation": "war-fulfilling"}, {"id": "autokranos-word6", "translation": "fate-fulfilling"}, {"id": "autokranos-word7", "translation": "war-fulfilling"}, {"id": "autokranos-word8", "translation": "overseer, pleasing"}, {"id": "autokranos-word9", "translation": "pleasing"}, {"id": "autoktitos-orth1", "translation": "self-built, natural"}, {"id": "autoktitos-def1", "translation": "self-built, natural"}, {"id": "autoktitos-note1", "translation": "Of caves made not by art but by nature"}, {"id": "autoktitos-note2", "translation": "αὐτοκτίτους δόμους [self-built houses] Sophocles said fr. 306."}, {"id": "autoktitos-quote1", "translation": "Rock-roofed, self-built caves."}, {"id": "autoktitos-word1", "translation": "self-built houses"}, {"id": "autoktonos-orth1", "translation": "self-slaying"}, {"id": "autoktonos-def1", "translation": "self-slaying"}, {"id": "autoktonos-note1", "translation": "In the plural number αὐτοκτόνοι [self-slaying] means slaying each other."}, {"id": "autoktonos-note2", "translation": "of the mutual slaughter of Eteocles and Polynices"}, {"id": "autoktonos-quote1", "translation": "The men are dead by self-slaying hands."}, {"id": "autoktonos-quote2", "translation": "And the death of the two brothers is thus self-slaying."}, {"id": "autoktonos-word1", "translation": "self-slaying"}, {"id": "autoktonos_adv-orth1", "translation": "by self-slaying"}, {"id": "autoktonos_adv-def1", "translation": "by self-slaying"}, {"id": "autoktonos_adv-note1", "translation": "Thus Triclinius for αὐτοκτόνωσιν [by self-slaying], which is in M, changed by a later hand to αὐτοὶ κτάνωσιν [they themselves may slay]."}, {"id": "autoktonos_adv-quote1", "translation": "Did you not dare to do this deed by self-slaying?"}, {"id": "autoktonos_adv-quote2", "translation": "When they die by self-slaying, slain by each other."}, {"id": "autoktonos_adv-word1", "translation": "by self-slaying"}, {"id": "autoktonos_adv-word2", "translation": "they themselves may slay"}, {"id": "autokopos-orth1", "translation": "with the very hilt"}, {"id": "autokopos-def1", "translation": "with the very hilt"}, {"id": "autokopos-note1", "translation": "of a brave man fighting hand-to-hand with the sword"}]}